  "caption_final": "Death Stranding 2: On the Beach joins the PlayStation Plus Game Catalogue on 17 November, Sony's PlayStation Blog said on Tuesday. The catalogue comes with the Extra and Deluxe tiers; Essential (₹649 a month in India) doesn't include it.\n\nIn India, PS Plus Extra costs ₹979 a month, ₹2,599 for three months or ₹8,709 a year, and Deluxe costs ₹1,109 a month. Buying the game outright costs ₹4,999 for the Standard Edition on PS Store India, or ₹3,099 in the store's current sale, which runs until 20 November.\n\nAtomfall and Dragon Quest III HD-2D Remake join on 17 November too. Sony gives US and UK dates for the rest: Hell Let Loose on 11 November; Like a Dragon: Pirate Yakuza in Hawaii, Trepang2, MotoGP 26 and Cricket 26 on 24 November. Deluxe adds Soul Reaver 2 and Freedom Wars Remastered. Sony says lineups can differ by region.\n\nDo you buy big PS5 games at launch, or wait for them to reach PS Plus?\n\nSources: PlayStation Blog, PlayStation India, Push Square, Digit, Gizmochina\n\n#DeathStranding2 #PSPlus #PlayStation #PS5 #idlynerd\n\nImage: PlayStation (Sony Interactive Entertainment)",
